  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "Last year a bicycle cost \\(\\$160\\) and a cycling helmet cost \\(\\$40.\\) This year the cost of the bicycle increased by \\(5\\%,\\) and the cost of the helmet increased by \\(10\\%.\\) The percent increase in the combined cost of the bicycle and the helmet is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(7\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(7.5\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(15\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The combined percentage increase compares the total dollar increase with last year's combined cost. The bicycle's increase is \\(160(0.05)=8\\) dollars, and the helmet's increase is \\(40(0.10)=4\\) dollars.\n\nLast year's combined cost was \\(160+40=200\\) dollars, so the percentage increase is\n\\[\n\\frac{8+4}{200}\\times100\\%=\\boxed{6\\%}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
